\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Six fitted fusions against the equal-weight rank average, on the released folds under the five-study protocol. None of the 30 paired differences has a 95\% interval that excludes zero. The widest are breast against the concatenation, $[-0.1399, +0.0010]$ at $p=0.054$, and colorectal against it, $[-0.0214, +0.1446]$. Each difference is the mean of its 6,000 bootstrap replicates, so it can differ in the last digits from the difference of the two concordances. Simplex weights, stacking with interactions and weights by clinical tertile were specified after the first two combinations had been scored, and the tuned-ridge stacking was added by amendment A2 (Supplementary Note~\ref {note:amendA2}).}}{7}{table.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:fusion}{{7}{7}{Six fitted fusions against the equal-weight rank average, on the released folds under the five-study protocol. None of the 30 paired differences has a 95\% interval that excludes zero. The widest are breast against the concatenation, $[-0.1399, +0.0010]$ at $p=0.054$, and colorectal against it, $[-0.0214, +0.1446]$. Each difference is the mean of its 6,000 bootstrap replicates, so it can differ in the last digits from the difference of the two concordances. Simplex weights, stacking with interactions and weights by clinical tertile were specified after the first two combinations had been scored, and the tuned-ridge stacking was added by amendment A2 (Supplementary Note~\ref {note:amendA2})}{table.7}{}}
