\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces ModRank, the clinical arm and the paired differences on the benchmark's five studies, 2,241 patients and 411 events. The clinical column is age, sex and pathologic stage from the clinical files released with the benchmark. Differences are paired at the patient level, and each is the mean of its 6,000 bootstrap replicates, which can differ in the last digits from the difference of the printed concordances. Against the clinical arm, the intervals that exclude zero are bladder $[+0.0298, +0.1267]$, breast $[+0.0519, +0.1897]$ and head and neck $[+0.0206, +0.1231]$. Against the grade arm, colorectal alone does, at $[+0.0437, +0.1429]$. No difference against the two-modality arm excludes zero in any study.}}{8}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
