\newlabel{tab:architectures}{{12}{12}{Four further architectures on the development cohort. Concordance is pooled over out-of-fold predictions of the rank average of five retrainings, with the mean and standard deviation of the five retrainings' own concordance beside it. Reported is the value SurvPath gives for the same folds, the mean of per-fold concordance rather than a pooled value. The last two columns are the added value over the grade-based and the stage-based reference}{table.12}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces The inflation $D$ against a score without information combined by the same rule. The point excess is $D$ minus the benchmark on the full data. The excess is the mean of 6,000 bootstrap replicates of $D$ minus the benchmark, averaged in each replicate over 20 random draws. The two differ where the bootstrap distribution is not centred on the full-data value, most in the cystectomy cohort. The five-study rows use that protocol's clinical file and a single penalty selection, as in Supplementary Note~\ref {note:fivecohort}. The external cohorts add the transcriptome to each reference.}}{12}{table.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:nulld}{{13}{12}{The inflation $D$ against a score without information combined by the same rule. The point excess is $D$ minus the benchmark on the full data. The excess is the mean of 6,000 bootstrap replicates of $D$ minus the benchmark, averaged in each replicate over 20 random draws. The two differ where the bootstrap distribution is not centred on the full-data value, most in the cystectomy cohort. The five-study rows use that protocol's clinical file and a single penalty selection, as in Supplementary Note~\ref {note:fivecohort}. The external cohorts add the transcriptome to each reference}{table.13}{}}
