\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces A stage-based against a grade-based clinical model in every cohort with a usable grade. The TCGA rows are the benchmark's own studies under the five-study protocol (Supplementary Note~\ref {note:fivecohort}). Breast and colorectal record no usable grade and are not shown. The other rows are external bladder cohorts, each on its own endpoint, which is disease-specific (DSS), overall (OS), cancer-specific (CSS) or progression-free survival to muscle invasion (PFS). MIBC and NMIBC are muscle-invasive and non-muscle-invasive disease. Entropy is grade's Shannon entropy normalised by its maximum, and C is the concordance of the stage-based and the grade-based clinical model. The gap is computed before rounding, so it can differ in the last digit from the difference of the two printed concordances.}}{13}{table.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:gapext}{{14}{13}{A stage-based against a grade-based clinical model in every cohort with a usable grade. The TCGA rows are the benchmark's own studies under the five-study protocol (Supplementary Note~\ref {note:fivecohort}). Breast and colorectal record no usable grade and are not shown. The other rows are external bladder cohorts, each on its own endpoint, which is disease-specific (DSS), overall (OS), cancer-specific (CSS) or progression-free survival to muscle invasion (PFS). MIBC and NMIBC are muscle-invasive and non-muscle-invasive disease. Entropy is grade's Shannon entropy normalised by its maximum, and C is the concordance of the stage-based and the grade-based clinical model. The gap is computed before rounding, so it can differ in the last digit from the difference of the two printed concordances}{table.14}{}}
